  "Notes": [
    "All batches use the unchanged EngineComparison harness, exact NuGet 3.2.8, the pinned .NET SDK/runtime, eight parallel modules, and three fresh-process repetitions per version and count. Each worker warms once, forces GC, then measures another asynchronously disposed pipeline.",
    "Workers and build artifacts reside on a native Linux Docker volume. Source is bound read-only from the Windows worktree. The container has a four-CPU quota and 4 GiB memory; every dotnet child retains the default 2 GiB guard. Existing development containers remain running; no other benchmark or build runs concurrently.",
    "The before batch reports SourceDirty=true because Linux Git initially lacked core.autocrlf for the CRLF Windows checkout. Windows git status was clean before the batch; its core source is the recorded d7c9eaab9d0e77424d71c3fdb4572c5a7faab1bb commit. Later batches set core.autocrlf=true and correctly report the initializer source patch as dirty. The normalized source hashes identify the before and after implementations.",
    "PeakWorkingSetBytes measures the worker lifetime high-water mark, including startup, JIT and warmup; child processes are excluded. It is not retained managed heap or process-tree RSS.",
    "The first after batch covers 50 commands. An independent confirmation repeats 50 commands and adds a 500-command control. The original metadata and individual samples below are preserved."
  ],
